2
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:22.020
Confirm the patient's identity, then explain the examination and gain consent to perform it.

3
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:30.520
Take a few seconds to observe the periorbita, eyelids and the eyes themselves, commenting on any positive or relevant negative findings.

4
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.618
The next step is to perform the fundal reflex test to assess for mediopacity.

5
00:00:34.618 --> 00:00:42.520
Set the arclight by clicking the button three times for the brightest light, and then move the lens rack to the top so there's no lens power.

6
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.671
With the arc light prepared, dim the lights in the room, and at arm's

7
00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:47.560
length, look through

8
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.560
the sighthole.

9
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.880
I asked the patient to look at the light, observing both eyes at the same time.

10
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.600
The light should reflect from the fundus back through the pupils, looking symmetrically

11
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.640
bright with similar colour.

12
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:04.360
Any asymmetry suggests an abnormality such as corneal scar, cataract, blood in the vitreus,

13
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.360
