14
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.920
Next examine the back of the eye.

15
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.160
I asked the patient to fix on a target in the distance.

16
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.173
Use your right hand and right eye to examine their right eye and your

17
00:01:15.173 --> 00:01:16.320
left for their left.

18
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.000
Start with your feet close to the patient and lean back, identify the fundal reflex and

19
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.680
follow this moving in on a path 10 to 15 degrees temporal on the horizontal.

20
00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.360
When you're close to the eye the optic disc should come into view, going closer still

21
00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.960
and you'll get a wider and more stable view.

22
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.476
Comment on how distinct the margin of the disc is, the colour of the

23
00:01:39.476 --> 00:01:40.480
